{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>A full year.</b> And if the year was intercalated, it is intercalated for him." "<b>In a city that has no wall.</b> Read לו (to it), for it refers back to 'field' — that was its state at the time of its wall. And 'field' is masculine, as it is written: והיה השדה בצאתו ביובל." "<b>No wall, לצמיתת.</b> In PaTḤaḥ, and its mnemonic companion: לקנה אתו."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {2 "The comment refers to the cantillation/traditional reading of לא; the phrase וחברו סימנו likely denotes a paired mnemonic sign for the accents. The text is terse and possibly elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:16.584404167Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}